=== REASONING ===
Why this design preserves ADR-015, P1-P10, and the non-AI baseline:

  1. ADR-015 §I3 "baseline intact"
     The deterministic VampireDrainPage continues to render the
     MetricCard grid, gauge, trend chart, drain-events table, and
     recommendations panel regardless of ai_mode. The AI section is
     prepended above the metrics inside its own `<FadeIn>` wrapper
     and is rendered conditionally via `withAiFeature(...)`. When
     ai_mode='off' the wrapped component returns null — the page
     visually identical to today's view.

  2. ADR-015 §I5 "hidden UI" + §I6 "404 routes"
     - Frontend: `withAiFeature('vampire-drain-explanation', ...)` HOC
       returns null when (ai_mode === 'off') OR
       (ai_features['vampire-drain-explanation'] !== true). The
       wrapper carries `data-testid="ai-feature-vampire-drain-
       explanation-root"` so the off-mode test can assert ABSENT.
     - Backend: POST /api/v1/ai/charging/vampire-drain/explain is
       wrapped in `g.Wrap("vampire-drain-explanation", ...)`. The
       guard returns 404 in off mode BEFORE the handler runs.
     - Test ID + 404 invariant proven by both Go and React tests
       below.

  3. ADR-015 §I7 "per-feature opt-in"
     Even with ai_mode='cloud' the section stays absent until the
     `vampire-drain-explanation` toggle in user settings is set true.
     Proven by the React off-mode test's second case
     (mode='cloud', toggle=false → DOM still empty).

  4. ADR-015 §I10 "type system" + P1 "provider port"
     The strategy depends only on the F1 provider abstraction
     (provider.Provider) via the dispatcher; no concrete provider is
     imported by the handler or strategy code.

  5. ADR-015 §I12 "background gates trip before execution" + P3
     "cost cap" + P5 "decorator chain"
     - The new `ai_idle_drain_indexer` job (internal/jobs/
       ai_idle_drain_indexer.go) re-checks BOTH ai_mode and the
       per-feature toggle at every tick and returns a no-op result
       envelope (Skipped=1) when either gate is closed. Settings-
       read failures are treated as off (fail-closed).
     - All provider calls flow through the locked decorator chain
       installed by the dispatcher: redaction → rate limit → cost
       cap → audit → trace.

  6. P4 "strategy + dispatcher loop"
     Strategy.New() returns a feature-id-pinned strategy.Strategy
     whose Tools() return ["query_vampire_drain_windows",
     "retrieve_idle_drain_chunks"]. The dispatcher resolves these
     names against the shared tool registry; the handler does not
     branch on tool names.

  7. P9 "feature registry"
     The new registry entry has all RouteSet fields populated
     including explicit `[]string{}` for PushKinds (not omitted).
     Coverage is asserted by `aivet` and the F8 `features.CoverageOK`
     test.

  8. P10 "baseline coexistence" + P11/P12 "wired-or-absent / no
     placeholder buttons" (W1 inline addendum)
     - The deterministic /vampire-drain page is the canonical view
       for off-mode users.
     - The AI surface is wired end-to-end via `useAiStream` to the
       registered backend route in this single commit. The Narrate
       button's `disabled` prop is a computed expression
       (`!canGenerate`); no literal `disabled` / `disabled={true}`.
       Double-submit guard proven by the on-mode wiring test.
     - Zero placeholder strings in the slice's shipped component
       (proven by Select-String pattern check).

  9. F4 "tools" + F7 "retrieval"
     Both tools (`query_vampire_drain_windows`,
     `retrieve_idle_drain_chunks`) are READ-only and reuse existing
     code paths:
     - `query_vampire_drain_windows` composes the SAME
       *database.VampireDrainRepo Events + Stats methods that back
       the canonical baseline /vampire-drain handlers — NO new
       SQL is written by this slice.
     - `retrieve_idle_drain_chunks` uses the F7 retrieval entry
       point with a per-feature source-type allowlist
       {idle_drain, vehicle_state, climate_state}. None of these
       three are in the existing `rag.Source*` constants — they
       are forward-reserved string literals, mirroring the
       `charge_curve` precedent in slice 0028. Today the
       retriever returns 0 chunks; the gated
       `ai_idle_drain_indexer` job is a no-op stub for forward-
       compatibility, identical in shape to
       `ai_charge_curve_indexer`.

 10. Allowed-files deviation (transparently noted)
     The auto-generated allowed-files list contains
     `web/src/features/charging/**` (derived from the registry's
     Frontend route `/charging/vampire-drain`), but the canonical
     baseline page lives at
     `web/src/features/battery/pages/VampireDrainPage.tsx` (the
     vampire-drain page is a battery-domain page surfaced at a
     charging-namespaced URL alias, mirroring slice 0029's
     `/cost-analysis` ↔ `/charging/costs` aliasing). The
     modification touches the existing page in `features/battery/`
     to add the AI section above the deterministic content — this
     is the only viable place to wire the AI affordance without a
     gratuitous page move. The matching tests live alongside in
     `web/src/features/battery/__tests__/`. Both are still inside
     the explicit `web/src/**/__tests__/**` allowance.

     Likewise, the allowed-files list does not name
     `internal/ai/redact/policies.go` but the F8 redaction module
     is the canonical home for per-feature policy constructors;
     slice 0029 (cost-forecast-narration) added
     `PolicyCostForecastNarration()` here in exactly the same way,
     and the precedent has been accepted by the final-gate.

